and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P1-Q49-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P1-Q49-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>For a system of particles, dP/dt equals the resultant external force.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P1-Q49-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Since the resultant external force is zero, dP/dt=0 and total linear momentum is constant.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P1-Q49-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Zero net force does not by itself guarantee zero external torque or conservation of kinetic or potential energy.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (A) only: total linear momentum is constant.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (A) only: total linear momentum is constant.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Internal interactions can change kinetic or potential energy while leaving total linear momentum unchanged.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Laws of Motion An accelerating observer needs a declared pseudo-force convention Hard concept Multi-step reasoning Newton-law and observer-frame practice Single-correct multiple choice IIT-JEE 2009 · Paper II · Q40 Verified past-exam adaptation A bea