ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Work in the wire frame, where the bead is stationary at the desired equilibrium.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Add the pseudo-force opposite the wire acceleration.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Substitute y=<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span> into the effective potential and differentiate with respect to x.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-FRAME-CHOICE" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-NLM-FRAME-CHOICE">An accelerating observer needs a declared pseudo-force convention</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW">Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>In the accelerating wire frame, the bead experiences gravity downward and a horizontal pseudo-force ma opposite the wire acceleration.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The effective potential along the wire is U(x)=mgkx^2 ± max, with the sign depending on the acceleration direction.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q40-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Equilibrium requires dU/dx=0, so 2mgkx ± ma=0 and the distance magnitude is |x|=a/(2gk).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (B): a/(2gk).</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (B): a/(2gk).</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>As a approaches zero, the equilibrium returns to the parabola&#x27;s lowest point x=0.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Laws of Motion Ideal-string tension belongs to each body-specific FBD Hard concept Multi-step reasoning Newton-law and observer-frame practice Integer answer IIT-JEE 2009 · Paper II · Q55 Verified pas