 type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 6/10 · about 2 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Requires solving the connected-body acceleration and tension before applying work over the first-second displacement.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A light inextensible string passes over a smooth fixed pulley and connects masses 0.36 kg and 0.72 kg. The system is released from rest. Taking g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, find the work in joules done by the string on the 0.36 kg block during the first second.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>String is light and inextensible.</li><li>Pulley is smooth.</li><li>The system starts from rest.</li><li>Use g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Using T=mg or using the heavy block&#x27;s weight difference directly as the work-producing force.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Solve the two-mass Atwood acceleration for the common string motion.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use Newton II on the 0.36 kg block to determine T.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Find its first-second displacement and take W=T s.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-IDEAL-STRING-TENSION" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-NLM-IDEAL-STRING-TENSION">Ideal-string tension belongs to each body-specific FBD</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-CONNECTED-COMMON-ACCEL" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-NLM-CONNECTED-COMMON-ACCEL">Connected bodies and a justified common acceleration</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" href="#g9-CORE1A--MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW">Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The common acceleration is a=(0.72-0.36)g/(0.72+0.36)=10/3 m/s^2.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>For the 0.36 kg block moving upward, T-mg=ma, so T=0.36(10+10/3)=4.8 N.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2009-P2-Q55-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Its displacement in the first second is s=(1/2)at^2=5/3 m, and string tension acts along the displacement, so W=Ts=4.8×5/3=8 J.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 8 J.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>8 J.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The work is positive on the lighter block because its displacement is in the same direction as the tension force.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Laws of Motion Quantitative static and kinetic friction conditions Hard concept Multi-step reasoning Newton-law and observer-frame practice Integer answer JEE Main 2026 · 06 Apr · Shift 2 · Q46 Verified past-exam adaptation A block takes time t to slide from rest down a 45° inclined plane. When the same plane is made frictionless, the time becomes t/2. If the original coefficient of friction is alpha/100, find alpha. The block starts from rest in both cases and traverses the same distance along the plane." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE Main · 2026 · Session 2 · 06 Apr 2026 · Shift 2 · Q46</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-NLM-FIRST-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="Laws of Motion"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Laws of Motion</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-FRICTION-QUANT" data-g9-meta-value="Quantitative static and kinetic friction conditions"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Quantitative static and kinetic friction conditions</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-FRICTION-QUANT" data-g9-meta-value="HARD"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Hard concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-NLM-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Newton-law and observer-frame practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Newton-law and observer-frame practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-meta-value="integer_answer"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Integer answer</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-meta-value="JEE Main 2026 · 06 Apr · Shift 2 · Q46"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE Main 2026 · 06 Apr · Shift 2 · Q46</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-06APR-S2-Q46" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s3f8e59f4b2fe7c5705bf878bbd494ccdf/uploads/2026/04/20260409725707538.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-comp