-btn g9-btn-practice active" href="core2.html">✍️ Practice</a><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-qb" href="../../../question-bank/index.html?capability=CAP-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">All questions in QB &rarr;</a></div></div></div><noscript>Answers open after you attempt; this page needs JavaScript.</noscript><main><h1>Two-dimensional kinematics and projectile model: Source questions</h1><article id="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Integer answer IIT-JEE 2011 · Paper II · Q33 Verified past-exam adaptation Inside a train accelerating uniformly along a straight track, a boy throws a ball forward at 10 m/s relative to the train and 60 degrees above the horizontal. To catch it again at the launch height he moves 1.15 m forward inside the train. Using g=10 m/s^2, find the train acceleration in m/s^2. Throw speed is relative to the train. Train acceleration is constant. Catch occurs at the original vertical level." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>IIT-JEE · 2011 · Paper II · Q33</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-meta-value="integer_answer"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Integer answer</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-meta-value="IIT-JEE 2011 · Paper II · Q33"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>IIT-JEE 2011 · Paper II · Q33</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2011_2.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Combines a projectile event clock with accelerated relative horizontal displacement.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>Inside a train accelerating uniformly along a straight track, a boy throws a ball forward at 10 m/s relative to the train and 60 degrees above the horizontal. To catch it again at the launch height he moves 1.15 m forward inside the train. Using g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, find the train acceleration in m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Throw speed is relative to the train.</li><li>Train acceleration is constant.</li><li>Catch occurs at the original vertical level.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Treating the train as constant-velocity and using only the ball&#x27;s horizontal component.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use the vertical return-to-launch-height condition to find the one common catch time.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Write ball-minus-train horizontal displacement over that same interval.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Set the relative displacement equal to the boy&#x27;s 1.15 m motion.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION">Apply constant-acceleration kinematics component by component</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Vertical motion fixes the common flight time: T=2(10 sin60)/10=sqrt(3) s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Relative horizontal displacement in the accelerating train is (10 cos60)T - (1/2)aT^2.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q33-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Set this equal to 1.15 m: 5sqrt(3) - 1.5a = 1.15, giving a≈5 m/s^2.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 5 m/s^2.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>5 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>For a=5, the relative displacement is about 1.16 m, consistent with the stated 1.15 m after rounding.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Connected reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2018 · Paper 2 · Q8 Verified past-exam adaptation A ball is launched from level ground at 45 degrees and reaches a maximum height of 120 m. At its first impact with the ground it loses half its kinetic energy. Immediately after the bounce its velocity is at 30 degrees above the horizontal. Find the new maximum height. First flight starts and ends at ground level. Half the kinetic energy is lost at the first bounce. Post-bounce launch angle is 30 degrees." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2018 · Paper 2 · Q8</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-meta-value="D2"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Connected reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-meta-value="numerical_value"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Numerical value</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2018 · Paper 2 · Q8"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2018 · Paper 2 · Q8</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2018_2.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D2">D2 · 5/10 · about 2 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Requires translating energy loss into speed and then extracting the new vertical component.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>0/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A ball is launched from level ground at 45 degrees and reaches a maximum height of 120 m. At its first impact with the ground it loses half its kinetic energy. Immediately after the bounce its velocity is at 30 degrees above the horizontal. Find the new maximum height.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>First flight starts and ends at ground level.</li><li>Half the kinetic energy is lost at the first bounce.</li><li>Post-bounce launch angle is 30 degrees.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Halving the speed instead of halving speed squared when kinetic energy halves.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use H=<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{y}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>/(2g) to infer the original vertical component.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>A 50% kinetic-energy loss means what happens to speed squared?</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use only the post-bounce vertical component to get the new maximum height.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Initial maximum height gives u_y^2=2g(120). At 45 degrees, u^2=2u_y^2=480g.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>After losing half the kinetic energy, the speed squared becomes v^2=u^2/2=240g.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2018-P2-Q08-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The new vertical speed squared is v^2 sin^2 30 = 60g, so H&#x27;=60g/(2g)=30 m.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 30 m.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>30 m.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The post-bounce height is one quarter of 120 m, consistent with half energy and a smaller vertical fraction.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2019 · Paper 2 · Q9 Verified past-exam adaptation A projectile is launched from the ground at speed u0 and angle theta. After each landing it rebounds at the same angle but with speed reduced by a constant factor alpha: u0/alpha, u0/alpha^2, and so on. If the magnitude of average velocity over the entire sequence is 0.8 times the magnitude V1 of the average velocity over the first flight, find alpha. Every rebound uses the same angle theta. Successive launch speeds form u0/alpha^n. The sequence continues indefinitely." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2019 · Paper 2 · Q9</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-meta-value="numerical_value"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Numerical value</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2019 · Paper 2 · Q9"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2019 · Paper 2 · Q9</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2019_2_English.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Requires recognizing two different geometric series, for range and time, before taking their ratio.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A projectile is launched from the ground at speed u0 and angle theta. After each landing it rebounds at the same angle but with speed reduced by a constant factor alpha: u0/alpha, u0/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">alpha^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and so on. If the magnitude of average velocity over the entire sequence is 0.8 times the magnitude V1 of the average velocity over the first flight, find alpha.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Every rebound uses the same angle theta.</li><li>Successive launch speeds form u0/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">alpha^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li><li>The sequence continues indefinitely.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Averaging the speeds of the flights instead of total displacement divided by total time.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>For fixed theta, determine how range and flight time scale with launch speed.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Write one geometric series for all ranges and a different one for all flight times.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Divide the two sums and compare with the first-flight average velocity.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>For a fixed launch angle, each flight time is proportional to speed and each range is proportional to speed squared.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Total displacement is R1[1+alpha^-2+alpha^-4+...] while total time is T1[1+alpha^-1+alpha^-2+...].</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2019-P2-Q09-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Thus V_avg/V1 = [1/(1-alpha^-2)]/[1/(1-alpha^-1)] = alpha/(alpha+1)=0.8, giving alpha=4.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 4.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>4.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>alpha=4 gives 4/5=0.8 exactly.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Connected reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q5 Verified past-exam adaptation A projectile is launched from ground at 5sqrt(2) m/s, at 45 degrees from the vertical. At the highest point it splits into two equal masses. One fragment falls vertically to the ground 0.5 s after splitting. The other fragment reaches the ground t seconds after splitting. Find t. g=10 m/s^2. The split occurs at the apex. Fragments have equal mass." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2021 · Paper 1 · Q5</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="D2"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Connected reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="numerical_value"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Numerical value</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q5"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q5</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2021_1_English.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D2">D2 · 4/10 · about 2 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" class="g9-why" hidden><p>The split event must be separated from the vertical free-fall event shared by the fragments.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>0/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A projectile is launched from ground at 5<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span> m/s, at 45 degrees from the vertical. At the highest point it splits into two equal masses. One fragment falls vertically to the ground 0.5 s after splitting. The other fragment reaches the ground t seconds after splitting. Find t.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li><li>The split occurs at the apex.</li><li>Fragments have equal mass.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Recomputing a full projectile flight from launch instead of starting the post-split clock at the apex.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="2"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Treat the split as a new initial condition at the apex, where the original projectile&#x27;s vertical velocity is zero.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Find the apex height from u_y, then ask what initial vertical velocity lets a fragment fall that height in exactly 0.5 s.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Resolve the launch: 5√2 m/s at 45° from the vertical gives u_x = u_y = 5 m/s. The apex is at t = u_y/g = 0.5 s, at height H = u_y²/2g = 25/20 = 1.25 m, where the velocity is (5, 0) m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> Follows from the gravity-only projectile model and momentum conservation at the split, as shown in this step.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Apex at 0.5 s, H = 1.25 m, velocity (5, 0) m/s.</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The fragment that falls vertically covers 1.25 m in 0.5 s. From rest, a 1.25 m fall takes √(2H/g) = √(2.5/10) = 0.5 s, so that fragment starts from rest: zero vertical and zero horizontal velocity just after the split.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> Follows from the gravity-only projectile model and momentum conservation at the split, as shown in this step.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> The vertical fragment starts from rest at the split.</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q05-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Momentum at the split: before, M(5, 0) m/s. After, (M/2)(0, 0) + (M/2)v₂, so v₂ = (10, 0) m/s. The other fragment also starts with zero vertical velocity from 1.25 m, so it lands after t = √(2H/g) = 0.5 s (at x = 2.5 + 10 × 0.5 = 7.5 m from the launch point).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> Follows from the gravity-only projectile model and momentum conservation at the split, as shown in this step.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 0.5 s.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>0.5 s.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Vertical momentum is zero before the split and both fragments have zero vertical velocity after it, so vertical momentum is conserved (0 = 0); both then fall 1.25 m from rest in the same 0.5 s, and horizontal momentum M × 5 = (M/2) × 10 checks the second fragment&#x27;s speed.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q6 Verified past-exam adaptation Use the same projectile-splitting setup as Q5: launch speed 5sqrt(2) m/s at 45 degrees from vertical; at the apex it splits into equal masses and one fragment drops vertically, reaching ground 0.5 s later. Find the horizontal distance x from the launch point at which the other fragment lands. g=10 m/s^2. Equal fragments. One fragment has zero horizontal velocity immediately after splitting." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2021 · Paper 1 · Q6</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="numerical_value"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Numerical value</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q6"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2021 · Paper 1 · Q6</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2021_1_English.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 6/10 · about 2 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Combines projectile timing with momentum conservation at an internal fragmentation event.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>Use the same projectile-splitting setup as Q5: launch speed 5<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span> m/s at 45 degrees from vertical; at the apex it splits into equal masses and one fragment drops vertically, reaching ground 0.5 s later. Find the horizontal distance x from the launch point at which the other fragment lands.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>g=10 m/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li><li>Equal fragments.</li><li>One fragment has zero horizontal velocity immediately after splitting.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Assigning the second fragment the original 5 m/s horizontal speed instead of conserving momentum.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Find where the original projectile reaches its apex using its 5 m/s horizontal component.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>At the split, conserve horizontal momentum between the two equal fragments.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use the Q5 post-split fall time for the surviving fragment&#x27;s horizontal travel.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The original horizontal speed is 5 m/s and the apex time is 0.5 s, so the split occurs at x=2.5 m.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Horizontal momentum just before splitting is M·5. If one equal fragment has zero horizontal speed, the other equal fragment must have horizontal speed 10 m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2021-P1-Q06-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>During the 0.5 s post-split fall it travels another 5 m horizontally, so x=2.5+5=7.5 m.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 7.5 m.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>7.5 m.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Horizontal momentum at the split is conserved: (M/2)·0 + (M/2)·10 = M·5.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2024-P2-Q09" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Non-negative integer JEE (Advanced) 2024 · Paper 2 · Q9 Verified past-exam adaptation A ball is thrown from (0,0) with fixed speed v0 at angle theta0. Simultaneously, a stone is thrown from (L,0) toward the ball at angle 180°-theta1 with a suitable speed. For (theta0,theta1)=(45°,45°) the hit occurs after T1; for (60°,30°) it occurs after T2. Find (T1/T2)^2. Both projectiles are launched simultaneously from the same vertical level. Gravity is common to both particles. The stone&#x27;s speed is chosen so that collision occurs." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2024 · Paper 2 · Q9</h2><p c