" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A projectile has ordinary range d when launched at speed v and angle theta under gravity g. At the highest point it enters a region where the effective downward acceleration is g/0.81. If its new total horizontal range is d&#x27;=n d, find n.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>The acceleration changes only after the projectile reaches its apex.</li><li>Horizontal velocity is unchanged at the boundary.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Recomputing the whole flight with the modified gravity instead of changing only the descent.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use symmetry only for the ordinary projectile to identify the apex position.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Compare the fall time from a fixed height under g and g/0.81.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Convert that time ratio into the second-stage horizontal distance.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The projectile reaches the apex after covering half of its ordinary range, d/2.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The apex height is unchanged, but the downward acceleration becomes g/0.81, so the fall time from the apex is 0.9 times the original descent time.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2022-P1-Q08-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The second horizontal segment is therefore 0.9(d/2); hence d&#x27;=d/2+0.9d/2=0.95d.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 0.95.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>0.95.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Stronger effective gravity must shorten only the post-apex horizontal segment, so n must lie between 0.5 and 1.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept High-transfer / exception-sensitive Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Multiple-correct multiple choice JEE (Advanced) 2023 · Paper 1 · Q1 Verified past-exam adaptation A ball slides without friction from a height h above a terrace whose top is 3h above the ground, leaves horizontally, strikes the ground and rebounds with coefficient of restitution 1/sqrt(3). Determine which of the source statements about launch speed, impact angle, rebound velocity and rebound geometry are correct. Slide is frictionless. Ground is horizontal. Coefficient of restitution is 1/sqrt(3). x-hat points horizontally in the direction the ball leaves the terrace, and z-hat points vertically upward. (A) u0=sqrt(2gh) horizontally (B) rebound velocity equals sqrt(2gh)(x-hat - z-hat) (C) impact angle is 60 degrees (D) horizontal range divided by rebound maximum height is 2sqrt(3)" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2023 · Paper 1 · Q1</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-meta-value="D4"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>High-transfer / exception-sensitive</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-meta-value="multi_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multiple-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2023 · Paper 1 · Q1"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2023 · Paper 1 · Q1</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2023_1_English.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D4">D4 · 8/10 · about 4 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Chains energy, projectile motion and restitution across two events.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A ball slides without friction from a height h above a terrace whose top is 3h above the ground, leaves horizontally, strikes the ground and rebounds with coefficient of restitution 1/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. Determine which of the source statements about launch speed, impact angle, rebound velocity and rebound geometry are correct.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Slide is frictionless.</li><li>Ground is horizontal.</li><li>Coefficient of restitution is 1/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</li><li>x-hat points horizontally in the direction the ball leaves the terrace, and z-hat points vertically upward.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Losing the sign of the rebound vertical velocity or mixing launch/drop heights.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use energy conservation on the slide to get the horizontal launch speed.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Find the vertical impact component from the 3h fall.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Apply restitution to the vertical component, then compute rebound height and compare with the first-flight range.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Energy on the slide gives horizontal launch speed u0=sqrt(2gh).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Falling through 3h gives vertical impact speed sqrt(6gh), so tan(theta)=sqrt(6gh)/sqrt(2gh)=sqrt(3), hence theta=60 degrees.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2023-P1-Q01-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>After impact the upward vertical component is sqrt(2gh); rebound height is h, while pre-impact flight gives horizontal distance 2sqrt(3)h, so d/h1=2sqrt(3).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Options (A), (C) and (D).</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Options (A), (C) and (D).</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The restitution factor maps the downward <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{6gh}</annotation></semantics></math></span> to an upward <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{2gh}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, so the rebound velocity is <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{2gh}</annotation></semantics></math></span>(x-hat + z-hat) with z-hat upward; option (B)&#x27;s (x-hat - z-hat) points downward and is not correct.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Apply constant-acceleration kinematics component by component Medium concept High-transfer / exception-sensitive Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Numerical value JEE (Advanced) 2025 · Paper 2 · Q15 Verified past-exam adaptation A 0.2 kg projectile is launched at 270 m/s at 60 degrees in a medium with linear drag F=-c v, where c=0.1 kg/s. It hits a vertical wall after 2 s. Taking e=2.7 for the exponential evaluation specified by the source, determine the horizontal distance to the wall. Linear viscous drag acts opposite the instantaneous velocity. Use the source&#x27;s e=2.7 approximation." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2025 · Paper 2 · Q15</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION" data-g9-meta-value="Apply constant-acceleration kinematics component by component"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Apply constant-acceleration kinematics component by component</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-meta-value="D4"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>High-transfer / exception-sensitive</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-meta-value="numerical_value"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Numerical value</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2025 · Paper 2 · Q15"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2025 · Paper 2 · Q15</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2025_2_English.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D4">D4 · 8/10 · about 4 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Requires solving a velocity-dependent Newton-II equation and integrating the horizontal component.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A 0.2 kg projectile is launched at 270 m/s at 60 degrees in a medium with linear drag F=-c v, where c=0.1 kg/s. It hits a vertical wall after 2 s. Taking e=2.7 for the exponential evaluation specified by the source, determine the horizontal distance to the wall.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Linear viscous drag acts opposite the instantaneous velocity.</li><li>Use the source&#x27;s e=2.7 approximation.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Using constant-acceleration projectile formulas despite velocity-dependent drag.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Write Newton II for the horizontal component only.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Identify the decay time constant m/c.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Integrate vx(t) from 0 to 2 s rather than multiplying the final speed by time.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-CONSTANT-ACCELERATION">Apply constant-acceleration kinematics component by component</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The horizontal component obeys m dvx/dt=-c vx, so vx(t)=vx0 exp[-(c/m)t].</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Here vx0=270 cos60=135 m/s and m/c=2 s, so x(t)=vx0(m/c)[1-exp(-ct/m)].</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2025-P2-Q15-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>At t=2 s, x=270(1-1/e)=270(1-1/2.7)=170 m.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 170 m (within the official accepted interval 167–171 m).</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>170 m (within the official accepted interval 167–171 m).</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The distance is smaller than the no-drag value 135×2=270 m, as it must be.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept High-transfer / exception-sensitive Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Single-correct multiple choice IIT-JEE 2011 · Paper II · Q26 Verified past-exam adaptation A 0.2 kg ball rests on top of a 5 m vertical post. A 0.01 kg bullet moving horizontally with speed V strikes the ball centrally. After the collision the ball and bullet move independently and land 20 m and 100 m, respectively, from the foot of the post. Find the bullet&#x27;s initial speed. Both bodies begin their post-collision projectile motion from the same 5 m height. Use g=10 m/s^2 for the numerical evaluation consistent with the source options. (A) 250 m/s (B) 250sqrt(2) m/s (C) 400 m/s (D) 500 m/s" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="bl