">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Apply horizontal momentum conservation across the brief collision.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>From height 5 m with zero initial vertical velocity, the common fall time is t=sqrt(2h/g)=1 s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>Therefore the ball and bullet post-collision horizontal speeds are 20 m/s and 100 m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2011-P2-Q26-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Horizontal momentum during the short collision is conserved: 0.01V=0.2(20)+0.01(100)=5, giving V=500 m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated model, conservation law, or stoichiometric relation preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (D): 500 m/s.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (D): 500 m/s.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The two bodies have the same fall time because they leave from the same height with zero vertical velocity; their different ranges therefore directly encode different horizontal speeds.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Integer answer JEE (Advanced) 2014 · Paper 1 · Q11 Verified past-exam adaptation Airplanes A and B fly at constant velocities in the same vertical plane, at 30 degrees and 60 degrees to the horizontal. A moves at 100sqrt(3) m/s. At t=0, B is 500 m from A, and an observer in A sees B move perpendicular to A&#x27;s flight direction. If A just avoids being hit by B, find the encounter time t0. Both airplanes move with constant velocity. Their trajectories are straight lines in one vertical plane. Initial separation is 500 m." class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2014 · Paper 1 · Q11</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" data-g9-meta-value="Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-meta-value="integer_answer"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Integer answer</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2014 · Paper 1 · Q11"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2014 · Paper 1 · Q11</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2014_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Requires vector relative velocity plus a perpendicularity constraint before using the event separation.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>Airplanes A and B fly at constant velocities in the same vertical plane, at 30 degrees and 60 degrees to the horizontal. A moves at 100<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span> m/s. At t=0, B is 500 m from A, and an observer in A sees B move perpendicular to A&#x27;s flight direction. If A just avoids being hit by B, find the encounter time t0.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Both airplanes move with constant velocity.</li><li>Their trajectories are straight lines in one vertical plane.</li><li>Initial separation is 500 m.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Subtracting scalar speeds instead of velocity vectors.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Resolve both airplane velocities into horizontal and vertical components.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Impose <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{B}</annotation></semantics></math></span>/A · <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{A}</annotation></semantics></math></span> = 0.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>After finding relative speed, use the 500 m initial separation.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Resolve A&#x27;s velocity as (150, 50sqrt(3)) m/s. Let B&#x27;s speed be u, so its velocity is (u/2, u sqrt(3)/2).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The relative velocity v_B/A is perpendicular to A&#x27;s velocity. Their dot product is zero, which gives u=200 m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2014-P1-Q11-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Then v_B/A=(-50,50sqrt(3)) m/s, whose magnitude is 100 m/s. Closing 500 m at that relative speed gives t0=5 s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 5 s.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>5 s.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>500 m / 100 m/s = 5 s, matching the source answer.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Multiple-correct multiple choice JEE (Advanced) 2026 · Paper 1 · Q6 Verified past-exam adaptation A projectile launched from O with speed v at angle theta passes through P, which is 5 m horizontally and 1 m vertically from O. Determine which source statements are correct about the required speed and whether the projectile reaches its maximum height before or after P for specified launch angles. Uniform gravitational acceleration g acts downward. Point P has coordinates (5 m,1 m) relative to launch point O. (A) For theta=45°, v=5sqrt(g)/2 m/s (B) For theta=45°, maximum height is reached before P (C) For theta=30°, maximum height is reached after P (D) For theta=tan^-1(1/5), v=125sqrt(g) m/s" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2026 · Paper 1 · Q6</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="multi_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multiple-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2026 · Paper 1 · Q6"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2026 · Paper 1 · Q6</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/documents/p1_english.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Uses a prescribed point on a projectile trajectory plus apex-location reasoning across several launch angles.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A projectile launched from O with speed v at angle theta passes through P, which is 5 m horizontally and 1 m vertically from O. Determine which source statements are correct about the required speed and whether the projectile reaches its maximum height before or after P for specified launch angles.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Uniform gravitational acceleration g acts downward.</li><li>Point P has coordinates (5 m,1 m) relative to launch point O.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Checking only whether the point lies on the trajectory and not whether the apex occurs before or after it.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Substitute P=(5,1) into the projectile trajectory equation.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>For theta=45°, solve for v before assessing the apex.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use the trajectory slope or vertical velocity at x=5 to locate the apex relative to P.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="4"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Use y=x tan(theta)-g x^2/[2v^2 cos^2(theta)] at P=(5,1). For theta=45°, this gives v^2=25g/4, so v=5sqrt(g)/2; (A) is true.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>For the same 45° case, the slope of the path at x = 5 m is tan θ − g x/(v² cos² θ) = 1 − 5g/((25g/4)(1/2)) = 1 − 1.6 = −0.6 &lt; 0, so the projectile is already descending at P and the apex was passed before P; (B) is true.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>For θ = 30°: 1 = 5 tan 30° − 25g/(2v² cos² 30°) gives 25g/(1.5v²) = 2.887 − 1 = 1.887, so v² ≈ 8.83g. The slope at x = 5 m is tan 30° − 5g/(v² cos² 30°) ≈ 0.577 − 5/(8.83 × 0.75) ≈ 0.577 − 0.755 = −0.18 &lt; 0, so the apex is before P and (C) is false.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> (C) is false.</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="4" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2026-P1-Q06-MOVE-4" data-g9-solution-kind="VERIFY" data-g9-solution-stage="INTERPRET" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">4</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Interpret</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>For θ = tan⁻¹(1/5), the straight-line term x tan θ = 5 × 1/5 = 1 m already equals y at P, so the gravity term g x²/(2v² cos² θ) would have to be zero; no finite v does this, and (D) is false.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>θ = tan⁻¹(1/5)</li><li>P = (5 m, 1 m)</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the source-matched physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Options (A) and (B).</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Options (A) and (B).</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>The official final key marks AB.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Single-correct multiple choice JEE (Advanced) 2013 · Paper 1 · Q7 Verified past-exam adaptation A particle of mass m is projected from the ground with speed u0 at angle alpha. At the highest point of its trajectory it undergoes a completely inelastic collision with an identical particle that has been thrown vertically upward from the ground with the same initial speed u0. Find the angle made by the composite body with the horizontal immediately after collision. The first collision occurs at the highest point of the oblique projectile. The second particle has the same mass and the same launch-speed magnitude u0. The collision is completely inelastic. (A) pi/4 (B) pi/4 + alpha (C) pi/2 - alpha (D) pi/2" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE (Advanced) · 2013 · Paper 1 · Q7</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-meta-value="single_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Single-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-meta-value="JEE (Advanced) 2013 · Paper 1 · Q7"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE (Advanced) 2013 · Paper 1 · Q7</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2013_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 7/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Combines an apex projectile state, equal-height speed inference, and a completely inelastic vector-momentum collision.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>1/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>A particle of mass m is projected from the ground with speed u0 at angle alpha. At the highest point of its trajectory it undergoes a completely inelastic collision with an identical particle that has been thrown vertically upward from the ground with the same initial speed u0. Find the angle made by the composite body with the horizontal immediately after collision.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>The first collision occurs at the highest point of the oblique projectile.</li><li>The second particle has the same mass and the same launch-speed magnitude u0.</li><li>The collision is completely inelastic.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Using the second particle&#x27;s launch speed u0 as its collision speed instead of accounting for its rise to the collision height.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="free_response"><label>Your answer<textarea data-g9-attempt rows="4"></textarea></label><label class="g9-paper"><input data-g9-paper type="checkbox">I worked this on paper</label><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="3"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>At the first particle&#x27;s apex, write its remaining velocity component.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use the common collision height to determine the vertical particle&#x27;s speed there.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Add the two equal, perpendicular incoming momenta vectorially.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>At the first particle&#x27;s apex, its speed is purely horizontal with magnitude u0 cos(alpha).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from projectile energy/kinematics and momentum conservation in the source-matched collision.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>The collision height is H=u0^2 sin^2(alpha)/(2g). A second identical particle launched vertically upward from the ground with speed u0 has speed sqrt(u0^2-2gH)=u0 cos(alpha) at that height.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from projectile energy/kinematics and momentum conservation in the source-matched collision.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEADV-2013-P1-Q07-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The two equal masses therefore bring equal-magnitude perpendicular momenta into a completely inelastic collision, so the composite momentum bisects the right angle and makes angle pi/4 with the horizontal.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from projectile energy/kinematics and momentum conservation in the source-matched collision.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (A): pi/4.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (A): pi/4.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Both incoming momentum components have magnitude m u0 <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\cos (alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, so the post-collision resultant has equal horizontal and vertical components.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article><article id="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Motion in 2 D Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock Medium concept Connected reasoning Motion in 2D component and projectile practice Single-correct multiple choice JEE Main 2026 · 04 Apr · Shift 2 · Q29 Verified past-exam adaptation A projectile has coordinates x=24t and y=43.6t-4.9t^2, with x and y in metres and t in seconds. What angle does its velocity vector make with the horizontal at t=2 s? 60° 45° 30° 75°" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>JEE Main · 2026 · Session 2 · 04 Apr 2026 · Shift 2 · Q29</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-KIN-2D-MOTION" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2 D"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2 D</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" data-g9-meta-value="Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-meta-value="D2"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Connected reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-KIN-2D-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Motion in 2D component and projectile practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Motion in 2D component and projectile practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-meta-value="single_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Single-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-meta-value="JEE Main 2026 · 04 Apr · Shift 2 · Q29"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>JEE Main 2026 · 04 Apr · Shift 2 · Q29</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-e