lass="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Use <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\tan (theta)</annotation></semantics></math></span>=<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{y}</annotation></semantics></math></span>/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></span> only after evaluating both components at t=2 s.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="CONCEPT_NAV" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="concept_navigation"><h4>Need the concept again?</h4><ul><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-2D-INDEPENDENT-COMPONENTS">Split one plane-motion event into independent x/y components with one clock</a></li><li><a data-g9-concept-link data-g9-question-ref="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29" data-g9-concept-ref="MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL" href="core1a.html#MIC-PHY-KIN-PROJECTILE-MODEL">Select the gravity-only projectile model before using projectile consequences</a></li></ul></div></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Differentiate the coordinate laws: v_x=dx/dt=24 m/s and v_y=dy/dt=43.6-9.8t.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated source quantities and the preserved physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>At t=2 s, v_y=43.6-19.6=24 m/s.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated source quantities and the preserved physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-JEEMAIN-2026-04APR-S2-Q29-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Thus tan(theta)=v_y/v_x=1, so theta=45°.</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated source quantities and the preserved physical or chemical model.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> 45°.</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>45°.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>Equal positive horizontal and vertical velocity components at t=2 s require a 45° direction in the first quadrant.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article></main><footer data-g9-footer>Physics · Two-dimensional kinematics and projectile model</footer><script>\n(()=>{const q=(s,r=document)=>[...r.querySelectorAll(s)];\nconst store={get:k=>{try{return localStorage.getItem(\'g9-\'+k)}catch(e){return null}},set:(k,v)=>{try{localStorage.setItem(\'g9-\'+k,v);return true}catch(e){return false}},remove:k=>{try{localStorage.removeItem(\'g9-\'+k);return true}catch(e){return false}}};\nconst root=document.documentElement;const scope=root.dataset.g9Product