<a href="../../../physics/index.html">Physics</a><a href="../../../chemistry/index.html">Chemistry</a><a href="../../../mathematics/index.html">Mathematics</a><a href="../../../question-bank/index.html">Question Bank</a></nav><div class="g9-header-actions"><button type="button" class="g9-header-btn g9-search-btn" data-g9-action="search" title="Search Grade9V3 (Ctrl/⌘ K)" aria-label="Search"><span class="g9-btn-icon">🔍</span><span class="g9-btn-text">Search</span></button><button type="button" class="g9-header-btn g9-display-btn" data-g9-action="display" title="Display & Theme Settings" aria-label="Display & Theme"><span class="g9-btn-icon">🌙 / ☀️</span><span class="g9-btn-text">Display</span></button><a class="g9-header-btn" data-g9-action="pdf" href="core2.pdf" title="Open the PDF of this page to print it">PDF</a></div></div><div data-g9-search-panel hidden><input data-g9-search-input type="search" aria-label="Search this page"></div><div data-g9-display-panel hidden><button type="button" data-g9-font="dec">A-</button><button type="button" data-g9-font="reset">A</button><button type="button" data-g9-font="inc">A+</button><button type="button" data-g9-theme="light">Light</button><button type="button" data-g9-theme="dark">Dark</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="dec">Zoom -</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="reset">100%</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="inc">Zoom +</button></div></header><div class="g9-concept-triad-bar"><div class="g9-triad-inner"><div class="g9-triad-context" aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="../../../index.html">Home</a> / <a href="../../../physics/index.html">Physics</a> / <a href="../../../topics/nlm/index.html">Force and laws of motion</a> / <span aria-current="page">Practice</span></div><span class="g9-triad-concept-title">Concept: Force and laws of motion</span><div class="g9-triad-actions"><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-learn" href="core1a.html">📖 Learn</a><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-practice active" href="core2.html">✍️ Practice</a><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-qb" href="../../../question-bank/index.html?capability=CAP-NLM-SECOND-LAW">All questions in QB &rarr;</a></div></div></div><noscript>Answers open after you attempt; this page needs JavaScript.</noscript><main><h1>Force and laws of motion: Source questions</h1><article id="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Laws of Motion Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Newton-law and observer-frame practice Single-correct multiple choice IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3 Verified past-exam adaptation Two equal masses m lie on a smooth horizontal surface and are joined by a light string of total length 2a. The midpoint of the initially taut string is pulled vertically upward by a small constant force F. When the masses are separated by 2x, determine the magnitude of the acceleration of either mass. Horizontal surface is frictionless. String is light and remains taut. Each half-string has length a. (A) (F/2m)·a/sqrt(a^2-x^2) (B) (F/2m)·x/sqrt(a^2-x^2) (C) (F/2m)·x/a (D) (F/2m)·sqrt(a^2-x^2)/x" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>IIT-JEE · 2007 · Paper I · Q3</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-NLM-FIRST-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="Laws of Motion"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Laws of Motion</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-NLM-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Newton-law and observer-frame practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Newton-law and observer-frame practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="single_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Single-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2007_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 6/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Changing string geometry must be translated into tension components before Newton II is applied.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>0/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>Two equal masses m lie on a smooth horizontal surface and are joined by a light string of total length 2a. The midpoint of the initially taut string is pulled vertically upward by a small constant force F. When the masses are separated by 2x, determine the magnitude of the acceleration of either mass.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Horizontal surface is frictionless.</li><li>String is light and remains taut.</li><li>Each half-string has length a.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Taking T=F/2 without resolving the angled string segments.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="single_choice"><div class="g9-answer-options" data-g9-block="options"><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="0"><span>(A) (F/2m)·a/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="1"><span>(B) (F/2m)·x/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="2"><span>(C) (F/2m)·x/a</span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="3"><span>(D) (F/2m)·<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>/x</span></label></div><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="6"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_hints"><h4>Source support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-SOURCE_HINT" data-g9-support-group="SOURCE_HINT"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-SOURCE_HINT-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="SOURCE_HINT" data-g9-support-source="hints[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>How does the vertical displacement relate to half-string length and half-separation?</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-SOURCE_HINT-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="SOURCE_HINT" data-g9-support-source="hints[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>At the pulled midpoint, which components of the two equal tensions balance the applied force?</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-SOURCE_HINT-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="SOURCE_HINT" data-g9-support-source="hints[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>What horizontal force acts on either mass, and how does Newton’s second law determine its acceleration?</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show source hint</button></div></div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="authored_core2_support"><h4>Guided support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-group="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-1"><li data-g9-rung="1" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[0]" data-g9-support-reveals="CONCEPT" data-g9-support-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-1"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Represent</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>Sketch one half-string as a right triangle with horizontal projection x and vertical rise y.</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-2"><li data-g9-rung="2" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[1]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-2"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Connect</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>At the pulled midpoint, which components of the two equal tensions balance F?</p></div></li></template><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL-3"><li data-g9-rung="3" data-g9-support-provenance="AUTHORED_CORE2_PROMPT_REVEAL" data-g9-support-source="scaffolds[2]" data-g9-support-reveals="METHOD" data-g9-support-kind="EXECUTE" data-g9-supports-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-3"><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Carry out</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-guided">Guided</span></div><div data-g9-support-reveal><p>After finding T, resolve only its horizontal component on either mass.</p></div></li></template><button type="button" data-g9-next-rung>Show guided support</button></div></div></div></details></div></section></div></div><section class="blueprint-slot slot-solution" data-blueprint-slot="solution" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure" data-g9-component="SOLUTION" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE"><details data-g9-reveal data-requires-attempt data-g9-payload-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-solution"><summary>Answer and working</summary><div data-g9-payload-slot></div></details><template data-g9-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-solution"><div class="g9-component g9-c-step-list" data-g9-component="SOLUTION_STEPS" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEP_LIST" data-g9-component-items="3"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="structured_working"><h4>Reasoning route</h4><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="1" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-1" data-g9-solution-kind="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-stage="REPRESENT" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">1</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Represent</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>Let the midpoint rise by y. String geometry gives x^2 + y^2 = a^2, so y = sqrt(a^2-x^2).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 1</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="2" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-2" data-g9-solution-kind="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-stage="CONNECT" data-g9-solution-crux="true"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">2</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Connect</h4><p class="g9-prov" data-g9-crux-label>Key move</p><p data-g9-solution-action>At the massless midpoint, vertical force balance gives 2T(y/a)=F, hence T=Fa/(2y).</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> intermediate result 2</p></div></section><section class="g9-solution-move" data-g9-solution-order="3" data-g9-solution-move="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-MOVE-3" data-g9-solution-kind="TRANSFORM" data-g9-solution-stage="CALCULATE" data-g9-solution-crux="false"><div class="g9-step-no" aria-hidden="true">3</div><div class="g9-step-body"><h4 data-g9-solution-stage-label>Calculate</h4><p data-g9-solution-action>The horizontal force on either mass is T(x/a), so its acceleration is F x/[2m sqrt(a^2-x^2)].</p><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="solution_inputs"><h4>Uses</h4><ul><li>stated source quantities</li></ul></div><p data-g9-solution-why><em>Why valid:</em> This follows from the stated physical or chemical model and the quantities preserved in the source-matched task.</p><p data-g9-solution-output><strong>Result:</strong> Option (B): a_mass = F x / [2m sqrt(a^2-x^2)].</p></div></section></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-answer-box" data-g9-component="ANSWER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ANSWER_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="answer"><p>Option (B): <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{mass}</annotation></semantics></math></span> = F x / [2m <span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>].</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-check-box" data-g9-component="CHECK" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CHECK_BOX"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="independent_check"><h4>Independent check</h4><p>As x approaches zero, the horizontal acceleration approaches zero because the string segments become nearly vertical.</p></div></div></template></div></section></article></main><footer data-g9-footer>Physics · Force and laws of motion</footer><script>\n(()=>{const q=(s,r=document)=>[...r.querySelectorAll(s)];\nconst store={get:k=>{try{return localStorage.getItem(\'g9-\'+k)}catch(e){return null}},set: