tn" data-g9-action="display" title="Display & Theme Settings" aria-label="Display & Theme"><span class="g9-btn-icon">🌙 / ☀️</span><span class="g9-btn-text">Display</span></button></div></div><div data-g9-search-panel hidden><input data-g9-search-input type="search" aria-label="Search this page"></div><div data-g9-display-panel hidden><button type="button" data-g9-font="dec">A-</button><button type="button" data-g9-font="reset">A</button><button type="button" data-g9-font="inc">A+</button><button type="button" data-g9-theme="light">Light</button><button type="button" data-g9-theme="dark">Dark</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="dec">Zoom -</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="reset">100%</button><button type="button" data-g9-zoom="inc">Zoom +</button></div></header><div class="g9-concept-triad-bar"><div class="g9-triad-inner"><div class="g9-triad-context" aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="../../../public/index.html">Home</a> / <a href="../../../physics/index.html">Physics</a> / <a href="../../../topics/nlm/index.html">Force and laws of motion</a> / <span aria-current="page">Practice</span></div><span class="g9-triad-concept-title">Concept: Force and laws of motion</span><div class="g9-triad-actions"><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-learn" href="core1a.html">📖 Learn</a><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-practice active" href="core2.html">✍️ Practice</a><a class="g9-triad-btn g9-btn-qb" href="../../../question-bank/index.html?capability=CAP-NLM-SECOND-LAW">All questions in QB &rarr;</a></div></div></div><noscript>Answers open after you attempt; this page needs JavaScript.</noscript><main><section id="g9-role-CORE2" data-g9-role-section="CORE2"><h1>Force and laws of motion: Source questions</h1><article id="g9-CORE2--PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-unit="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-kind="QUESTION" data-g9-role="CORE2" data-g9-search-text="Physics Laws of Motion Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration Medium concept Multi-step reasoning Newton-law and observer-frame practice Single-correct multiple choice IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3 Verified past-exam adaptation Two equal masses m lie on a smooth horizontal surface and are joined by a light string of total length 2a. The midpoint of the initially taut string is pulled vertically upward by a small constant force F. When the masses are separated by 2x, determine the magnitude of the acceleration of either mass. Horizontal surface is frictionless. String is light and remains taut. Each half-string has length a. (A) (F/2m)·a/sqrt(a^2-x^2) (B) (F/2m)·x/sqrt(a^2-x^2) (C) (F/2m)·x/a (D) (F/2m)·sqrt(a^2-x^2)/x" class="g9-stage-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-identity" data-blueprint-slot="identity" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-header" data-g9-component="IDENTITY" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="HEADER"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_identity"><h2>IIT-JEE · 2007 · Paper I · Q3</h2><p class="g9-prov">Official past paper, faithful restatement of the original</p></div><div data-g9-meta-strip data-g9-meta-role="CORE2" data-g9-meta-record="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-search-safe><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="subject" data-g9-meta-ref="Physics" data-g9-meta-value="Physics"><strong>Subject:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Physics</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="topic" data-g9-meta-ref="BUCKET-PHY-NLM-FIRST-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="Laws of Motion"><strong>Topic:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Laws of Motion</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration"><strong>Concept:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Net force, not any one force, sets acceleration</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="concept-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="MIC-PHY-NLM-SECOND-LAW" data-g9-meta-value="MEDIUM"><strong>Concept difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Medium concept</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-difficulty" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="D3"><strong>Question difficulty:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Multi-step reasoning</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="family" data-g9-meta-ref="FAM-PHY-NLM-PRACTICE" data-g9-meta-value="Newton-law and observer-frame practice"><strong>Family:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Newton-law and observer-frame practice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="question-type" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="single_correct_mcq"><strong>Question type:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Single-correct multiple choice</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="source" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3"><strong>Source:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>IIT-JEE 2007 · Paper I · Q3</span></span><span data-g9-meta-item data-g9-meta-kind="provenance" data-g9-meta-ref="PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" data-g9-meta-value="PYQ_ADAPTED"><strong>Provenance:</strong> <span data-g9-meta-label>Verified past-exam adaptation</span></span></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-link-list" data-g9-component="SOURCE_PDF" data-g9-level="OPTIONAL" data-g9-presentation="LINK_LIST"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_pdf"><a class="g9-pdf-link g9-source-pdf" data-g9-source-pdf href="https://jeeadv.ac.in/past_qps/2007_1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" type="application/pdf" aria-label="Open the original past paper as a PDF to print it"><svg class="g9-pdf-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><path d="M6 2.5h8l4.5 4.5v14.5H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M14 2.5V7h4.5M9 12h6.5M9 15.5h6.5M9 19h4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source paper (PDF)</span></a></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-disclosure-grid" data-g9-component="DIFFICULTY_WHY" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="DISCLOSURE_GRID"><button type="button" class="g9-why-toggle" data-g9-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03"><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-band" data-g9-band="D3">D3 · 6/10 · about 3 min</span><span>Why this difficulty?</span></button><div id="g9-why-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" class="g9-why" hidden><p>Changing string geometry must be translated into tension components before Newton II is applied.</p><div class=g9-dgrid><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Choosing the model</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Representation</span><b>2/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Reasoning chain</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Algebra and numbers</span><b>1/2</b></div><div class="g9-dcell"><span>Traps and exceptions</span><b>0/2</b></div></div></div></div></section><div class="g9-split"><div class="g9-col g9-col-primary"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-attempt" data-blueprint-slot="attempt" data-required="true"><div class="g9-component g9-c-stem" data-g9-component="STEM" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="STEM"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Attempt first</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="stem"><p>Two equal masses m lie on a smooth horizontal surface and are joined by a light string of total length 2a. The midpoint of the initially taut string is pulled vertically upward by a small constant force F. When the masses are separated by 2x, determine the magnitude of the acceleration of either mass.</p></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-info" data-g9-component="CONDITIONS" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_INFO"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="conditions"><h4>Conditions</h4><ul><li>Horizontal surface is frictionless.</li><li>String is light and remains taut.</li><li>Each half-string has length a.</li></ul></div></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-callout-warn" data-g9-component="TRAP" data-g9-level="EXPECTED" data-g9-presentation="CALLOUT_WARN"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-wrong-route"><summary>Common wrong route · open if you want a warning</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="common_wrong_route"><h4>Common wrong route</h4><p>Taking T=F/2 without resolving the angled string segments.</p></div></div></details></div><div class="g9-component g9-c-attempt" data-g9-component="ATTEMPT" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="ATTEMPT"><div class="g9-attempt" data-g9-attempt-box data-g9-response-type="single_choice"><div class="g9-answer-options" data-g9-block="options"><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="0"><span>(A) (F/2m)·a/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="1"><span>(B) (F/2m)·x/<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="2"><span>(C) (F/2m)·x/a</span></label><label class="g9-answer-option"><input data-g9-choice type="radio" name="g9-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03" value="3"><span>(D) (F/2m)·<span class="katex"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>/x</span></label></div><button type="button" data-g9-commit>I have attempted this</button></div></div></section></div><div class="g9-col g9-col-support"><section class="blueprint-slot slot-representation" data-blueprint-slot="representation" data-required="false"></section><section class="blueprint-slot slot-support" data-blueprint-slot="support" data-required="false"><div class="g9-component g9-c-ladder" data-g9-component="HINT_LADDER" data-g9-level="REQUIRED" data-g9-presentation="LADDER" data-g9-component-items="6"><details class="g9-secondary-disclosure" data-g9-secondary="core2-hints"><summary>Need a hint? · guided support</summary><div class="g9-secondary-body"><div class="g9-eyebrow">Hint ladder · reveal only what you need</div><div class="g9-block" data-g9-block="source_hints"><h4>Source support</h4><div class="g9-ladder" data-g9-ladder-ref="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-IITJEE-2007-P1-Q03-SOURCE_HINT" data-g9-support-group="SOURCE_HINT"><ol data-g9-ladder></ol><ol class="g9-rung-map" aria-label="Rungs still to come"><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H0</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H1</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li><li data-g9-rung-ghost><div class="g9-rung-head"><span class="g9-rung-no">H2</span><span class="g9-rung-label" data-g9-support-stage-label>Support</span><span class="g9-pill g9-pill-source">Source</span></div></li></ol><template data-g9-rung-payload="CORE2-PYQ-PHY-